          { name: "Positioning Regional Economic Decline as Inevitable Rather Than Addressable", tag: "avoid", why: "Pennsylvania's post-industrial northeast faces genuine structural economic challenges—manufacturing decline, limited venture capital, geographic distance from major metros—that are real constraints on economic development. A representative who implicitly or explicitly communicates that decline is inevitable, or that the district's economic future is simply to manage decline rather than to grow, will lose credibility with younger adults and entrepreneurs who are still making decisions about whether to remain in or relocate from the area. Even if the honest assessment is constrained optimism, the message must emphasize active, strategic economic development engagement rather than passive management of decline." }
