          "Lead with working-class economic security in a district where $64,147 income and 30.9% renter rate signal housing burden and healthcare affordability as primary daily concerns — property tax fairness, rent affordability, and healthcare cost containment are more persuasive than identity-driven messaging in a constituency that is financially stretched.",
          "Engage the 30.9% renter population as a distinct constituency rather than absorbing them into a homeowner-majority narrative; older renters on fixed incomes and younger adults locked out of homeownership are both present in this rate, and both respond to housing and affordability messaging that acknowledges their material reality.",
          "Build persuasive contact with the persuadable center of the district rather than consolidating only existing Republican voters; in a seat where opposition reached 52%, assuming the existing base is sufficient is a strategic error — the candidate who reclaims this seat will be one who engages the 48-52 margin directly and credibly on material concerns."
