          { name: "Gun rights and Second Amendment interpretation", tag: "careful", why: "The 40% Republican share indicates a meaningful conservative constituency, and gun ownership is culturally significant in this region's communities. Candidates must acknowledge lawful gun ownership and sporting traditions while remaining consistent with district-wide support for the 60%-40% incumbent—overselling either restriction or absolutism risks alienating swing voters. Any gun messaging must center on specific, local public safety concerns, not national culture-war framing." },
          { name: "Immigration and border policy as national performance metrics", tag: "avoid", why: "Hispanic and Latino residents comprise only 2.44% of the district, and this population is too small to drive electoral outcomes. Emphasizing immigration as a salient local issue misreads this constituency's priorities and risks appearing tone-deaf to the bread-and-butter economic concerns that define the 60%-40% split. Candidates should focus on local and state-level economic and public safety issues where immigrant integration directly affects neighbors and businesses." },
          { name: "Social and cultural identity politics (abortion, LGBTQ+ issues as primary focus)", tag: "avoid", why: "The median age of 45.2 and stable residential patterns suggest a constituency less mobilized by cultural backlash messaging than by economic stability and family security. The 60% Democratic win indicates voters in this district chose the incumbent despite national cultural polarization, not because of it. Overplaying cultural grievance or identity-based messaging risks appearing to dismiss the kitchen-table concerns that actually drove turnout and persuasion in this specific electorate." }
