          "Engage the college-educated professional base on education funding, healthcare sustainability, and tax policy with policy specificity; this constituency evaluates on material governance outcomes, not inherited partisan loyalty, and a challenger who offers concrete fiscal stewardship would pose a real threat.",
          "Build specific visibility with the 16.8% non-white constituency (Black, Asian, Hispanic combined): these communities are present in meaningful numbers but risk becoming invisible in a district where the dominant narrative defaults to the white homeowner core, creating an opening for a challenger who engages them with authentic constituent attention.",
          "Address housing affordability and economic opportunity for the 39.8% renter population and younger adults; in a $73,964 median-income district, renters' housing costs relative to income are a real pressure point, and a challenger who makes this a campaign issue could mobilize a currently disengaged younger cohort."
