          "Lead on fiscal management and property tax fairness: in a 88% homeowner district with $132,482 median income, the constituency expects government to manage tax dollars efficiently, keep property taxes sustainable, and invest in education quality — these are the core competence signals that retain affluent suburban support.",
          "Do not concede education investment to the opposition: college-educated parents in high-income suburbs care deeply about education funding and quality, and a candidate who speaks only to tax cuts without addressing education sufficiency will lose credibility with this constituency's demographic core.",
          "Recognize that 57% is not a mandate: in a district this educated and affluent, a 43% opposition vote reflects real dissatisfaction among the constituency's college-educated swing voters — treating this as a safe seat rather than engaging the opposition's driving concerns is the fastest way to turn a 57% win into a vulnerability in the next cycle."
