          "Engage the college-educated professional constituency directly on what they actually evaluate: healthcare quality and cost, school performance, environmental quality, and whether government is run by people they perceive as competent and trustworthy — these are the material concerns of a 64%-college-educated, $151k-income constituency, not partisan litmus tests.",
          "Do not cede the property-owner and small-business constituency: the 81.3% homeownership rate and affluent profile mean that Republican messaging about property rights, reasonable taxation, and regulatory restraint resonates materially here — a Democratic incumbent must affirmatively address why their governance record protects rather than threatens these interests.",
          "Recognize that the 56% is not a landslide — it is a ten-point margin in a district where the demographic profile would predict a 60%+ Republican result: the gap between expected and actual partisan performance is the real story, and any challenger who can credibly make the case that the incumbent is misaligned with the district's competence and governance expectations has a viable path to a five-point swing."
