          { name: "Neglecting Constituent Service on Immediate Economic Pressures", tag: "avoid", why: "The district's 79% Democratic margin is built on material economic concerns — housing costs, healthcare access, wage stagnation, utility bills — not on abstract party loyalty or cultural positioning. Any legislative strategy that prioritizes symbolic politics, messaging victories, or culture-war issues over concrete constituent service and economic relief is actively undermining the foundation of the 79% result. For a working-class renter constituency with 36.7 median age facing real housing, healthcare, and wage pressures, legislative action on cost-of-living relief is not optional — it is the primary metric by which this constituency evaluates whether their representative is serving them. Neglecting this constituent service in favor of other legislative priorities is the fastest path to margin erosion." }
