          "Understand what the 33% Democratic vote represents: whether it is younger renters in the 22.9% segment, college-educated professionals with divergent cultural views, or simply urban Democratic base in an otherwise Republican area; whatever its composition, it is stable and unlikely to grow unless the Republican coalition fractures, but it is also unpersuadable and must be managed as a permanent opposition rather than a swing target.",
          "Lead on property tax management, school funding sufficiency, and rural/suburban infrastructure: at this income and homeownership level, the material governance concerns are tax burden, education quality, and whether roads and services keep pace with residential growth; these are the issues that differentiate an effective representative from an absent one.",
          "Avoid any messaging that signals cultural radicalism or departure from constituent expectations: in a district this stable and affluent, the opposition is concentrated among college-educated adults and younger renters who perceive cultural threat; Republican messaging that activates those perceptions unnecessarily may consolidate the 33% opposition rather than leaving any portion persuadable or low-propensity."
