          { name: "Treating Unopposed Status as Evidence of Secure Alignment", tag: "avoid", why: "The 2024 unopposed result reflects the current baseline Republican alignment and absence of a Democratic challenger, not permanent constituency commitment or durable electoral security. In a district where median age is 47.7 and material concerns center on property taxes and healthcare costs, an incumbent who relies on inherited partisan loyalty without building a visible record of legislative achievement on aging homeowner economic security is vulnerable to a future challenger who articulates concrete solutions. Unopposed status is an opportunity to build durable constituent relationships through delivery, not a signal that the seat will remain Republican regardless of incumbent performance or demographic shift." },
          { name: "Campaigning on Abstract Conservative Positioning Without Local Delivery", tag: "avoid", why: "A district with 47.7 median age, 70.5% homeownership, and $71,107 income evaluates its representative on concrete local delivery—property tax management, healthcare infrastructure, road maintenance, emergency services—not on conservative identity politics or abstract ideological positioning. An incumbent who campaigns on Republican brand loyalty without demonstrating specific legislative achievement on the material concerns that dominate aging homeowners' daily lives creates an opening for a Democratic challenger who articulates concrete solutions to healthcare costs, property tax burden, or infrastructure investment. This is a constituency that respects demonstrated competence and local problem-solving more than partisan affiliation." }
