          { name: "Partisan Positioning Without Material Constituency Service", tag: "avoid", why: "In a district where the median income is $67,765, 41.5% are renters, and college attainment is only 27.3%, voters are evaluating candidates on whether government is delivering concrete improvements to their economic lives — not on abstract partisan messaging or ideological positioning. An incumbent whose public profile emphasizes partisan credentials without demonstrating specific attention to housing affordability, workforce development, healthcare access, and cost-of-living relief will find that positioning vulnerable to a challenger who leads with material constituency service. This is a working-class district where practical governance and economic results matter more than party affiliation." }
