          "Defend the 69% by solving specific constituent problems: property tax fairness, healthcare cost management, and local service reliability are the material governance concerns for a 41.7-year-old, $63,799-income homeowner constituency — address these directly and publicly with measurable results rather than abstract policy positioning.",
          "Build constituent service infrastructure: with only 22% college-educated and a predominantly local information environment, direct communication, accessible constituent office responsiveness, and visible community presence matter more than media-dependent strategy — a representative who is genuinely accessible to constituents has structural protection against a primary or general election challenge.",
          "Do not treat the 5.6% demographic gap as negligible: identify the specific communities represented in that gap, engage them with tailored constituent attention, and ensure that immigrant communities, multiracial families, and non-majority populations feel represented rather than assumed into the Anglo homeowner narrative.",
          "Recognize that 69% is a strong current result, not a safe permanent floor: economic stress, service failures, or perceived unresponsiveness can erode this margin in a district this economically vulnerable — the margin is durable only if the incumbent demonstrates concrete commitment to the material concerns that generated it."
