          { name: "Taking the Constituency for Granted or Reducing Constituent Service Responsiveness", tag: "avoid", why: "An 82% margin can seduce an incumbent into believing that no engagement is necessary and that the seat is held indefinitely. This is strategically false; the margin reflects alignment on issues that matter to this constituency—property tax, infrastructure, municipal government effectiveness—and if the incumbent becomes perceived as non-responsive or as taking the district for granted, the consolidation that produced 82% can erode quickly to 65-70% in the face of a primary challenger or even a credible general election opponent who can argue that the incumbent is not fighting for working people's economic security." }
