          { name: "Higher Education & College Access", tag: "avoid", why: "Only 23.4% of adults are college-educated, well below the national average. Messaging that emphasizes college pathways, student debt relief, or research funding will land poorly and appear disconnected from district values. Conversely, vocational training, apprenticeships, and middle-skill job creation align with the district's actual workforce composition and should be the education focus if addressed at all." }
