          "Prevent minority community invisibility: Hispanic (3.96%), Black (2.78%), and Native American (~2.9%) communities are small but not negligible; their economic mobility concerns around wages, healthcare access, and education opportunity deserve specific constituent attention to prevent a challenger from mobilizing them around unaddressed grievances.",
          "Use the unopposed victory to build ahead: an unopposed race is an opportunity to deepen constituent relationships and identify emerging economic or social concerns before they organize into electoral opposition—active listening in year one and two of the term is far cheaper than crisis management in year three."
