          { name: "Ignoring the 4.3% Demographic Gap & Younger Cohort Shifts", tag: "avoid", why: "The gap between reported demographics (87.79% + 6.3% + 2.27% + 1.22% = 97.58%) leaves 2.42% unaccounted for, but more strategically important is the college-educated younger cohort at 26.9% that may not share the economic priorities or electoral assumptions of older homeowners. Campaigning this district as if the aging homeowner base is the only constituency that matters risks missing the emerging preference shifts among educated professionals who prioritize quality-of-life governance over inherited party loyalty." }
