          "Engage non-white and renter communities with specific constituent attention rather than token acknowledgment: the 14.29% non-white and 21% renter populations are small enough that they are often invisible in district strategy, but large enough that a credible challenger could mobilize them if the incumbent appears indifferent; early investment in genuine representation prevents this vulnerability.",
