          "Lead with homeowner economic concerns — property tax fairness, school funding adequacy, and the cost of local government — because 79.2% homeownership means these are not peripheral issues but the primary material concerns of the constituency.",
          "Address workforce development and job quality specifically for the 77% without college degrees; in a district where economic mobility depends on skilled trades and manufacturing employment, candidates who articulate a concrete vision for local job creation will resonate more than generic conservative or progressive positioning.",
          "Build constituent contact and visible presence in the district now, while unopposed; an incumbent who uses this period to establish deep local relationships, visibility at community events, and demonstrated constituent service will be much harder to challenge than one who becomes invisible between elections."
