          "Build authentic relationships with the ~4.2% demographic gap: Latino/a, Asian, and other minority residents in this district deserve direct engagement on economic mobility, healthcare access, and educational opportunity rather than being absorbed into a white working-class narrative that doesn't serve them.",
          "Sustain renter and younger adult engagement: the 32.7% renter rate represents households for whom housing costs are the dominant economic concern and whose voting behavior is more volatile than homeowners; concrete housing affordability policy and enforcement is more persuasive than partisan rhetoric.",
          "Do not treat unopposed victory as evidence of sustainable margins: a 43.0-year-old, working-class, white-majority district in Pennsylvania is a constituency where economic anxiety can be mobilized by a credible challenger if the incumbent has not delivered material improvements; active constituent service and concrete economic results are the foundation of durable Democratic support here."
