          { name: "Partisan Nationalization and Cultural Issues as the Primary Message", tag: "avoid", why: "PA-HD-114 is a district where an unopposed incumbent ran at 100%, creating risk of messaging that assumes Democrats will vote for any Democratic candidate purely on partisan grounds. Running a campaign centered on national partisan conflict, cultural issues, or ideological intensity rather than school funding, housing, and local economic growth is a pathway to mobilizing Republican opposition and activating persuadable suburban voters toward a challenger offering local solutions. The unopposed 2024 outcome should trigger incumbent caution about complacency, not confidence in partisan consolidation." },
          { name: "Treating the Incumbent's Unopposed Status as Evidence of District Safety", tag: "avoid", why: "An unopposed 2024 election is not evidence that PA-HD-114 is a durable Democratic district—it is evidence that local Republicans did not perceive sufficient opportunity to mount a challenge. In a district this close to suburban political competitiveness (83.5% white, moderate education levels, mixed renter-homeowner base), a Republican with credible local standing, specific messaging on schools and taxes, and genuine constituent relationships could quickly reframe the race and mobilize the 40% opposition baseline into a winning coalition. Incumbent strategy must anticipate this vulnerability, not ignore it." }
