          { name: "Treating 67% as a Permanent Floor", tag: "avoid", why: "A 67-33 margin in a district whose college-educated core (27.1% attainment) evaluates on governance competence and whose homeowner majority (83.9%) faces real economic pressure from healthcare costs and property taxes is not a secure baseline—it is a coalition that requires active maintenance through constituent responsiveness and competent administration. An incumbent who campaigns with the confidence of a landslide, neglects constituent service, or mismanages education or fiscal policy can find that 67% eroding to 60% or below in the next cycle if opposition mobilizes effectively around specific failures." }
