          "Lead with property tax and school funding competence: the 25.5% renter rate means 74.5% homeowners with direct stakes in property tax policy and school district quality; these are the swing voters who delivered the narrow 51% and who will evaluate based on whether government is delivering measurable results on these issues.",
          "Address cost-of-living pressures among affluent households: despite high income, suburban professionals at $105K are managing childcare costs, college savings, healthcare expenses, and housing affordability; messaging that acknowledges these real constraints rather than assuming material security is the incumbent's strongest consolidation strategy.",
          "Recognize the 49% as a genuinely mobilized opposition: in a high-income, college-educated district, 49% Republican support is substantial and reflects either strong Republican recruitment of educated voters or active dissatisfaction with Democratic performance on fiscal management — understand which before assuming the margin is safe."
