          "Serve the 11.09% Black and 7.64% Hispanic communities with specific constituent attention and concrete evidence of investment in their economic mobility, healthcare access, and safety — these communities are large enough to affect the outcome if they perceive the incumbent as taking their support for granted or underperforming on their material concerns.",
          "Engage the one-third renter constituency directly on housing affordability, wage growth, and opportunity — younger renters are the demographic group most likely to swing based on economic performance rather than inherited partisan alignment, and a credible alternative on housing and cost-of-living issues is the most dangerous vulnerability for the incumbent.",
          "Consolidate the college-educated homeowner majority by making a specific, evidence-based case on education funding, infrastructure, and tax fairness — this is the district's largest swing constituency, and they are sophisticated enough to evaluate competing claims and specific enough in their concerns that abstract messaging will not hold them."
