          "Lead with K-12 education quality and funding: in a district where 75.8% are college-educated and the median age includes young families, school performance, special education access, and whether the district's schools are delivering for an educated parent constituency are the primary quality-of-life issues that will determine electoral durability.",
          "Engage the 8.2% Asian community with specific attention to education access, anti-discrimination enforcement, and whether the district's institutions and decision-making reflect the actual demographic composition — this is a community that will reward representation with loyalty and punish invisibility with electoral exit.",
          "Build constituent relationships around fiscal governance and property-tax fairness: in a district with 75% homeownership and $167K income, the perceived relationship between property taxes paid and school/community services received is the primary fiscal concern; demonstrating fiscal competence and defending that relationship against tax-increase rhetoric is essential to electoral durability."
