          "Defend the 58% by demonstrating specific constituent service and legislative responsiveness — this is a high-engagement, high-information constituency that knows whether its representative is actually delivering on education, infrastructure, and fiscal management, and will punish perceived underperformance.",
          "Engage the Hispanic service and construction workforce community with specific attention to economic mobility, credential recognition, and healthcare access; in affluent suburbs, these communities can become invisible in district messaging despite being a meaningful part of the economy and constituency.",
          "Monitor for property-value and education-funding volatility as early warning indicators of margin erosion; affluent suburban Pennsylvania is sensitive to perceived threats to school quality and neighborhood stability, and any crisis in either can shift 3-4 percentage points of swing voters toward a credible challenger."
