          "Engage the white working-class 40.77% constituency specifically on jobs, healthcare access, and economic mobility — not as a separate coalition, but as part of a unified message about economic security that resonates across both Black and white working-class households simultaneously.",
          "Build early relationships with Black community institutions, labor unions, and grassroots organizations; the next challenger will mobilize through these networks, and an incumbent who consolidated unopposed status into authentic institutional relationships is far more durable than one who relied on ballot position alone."
