          "Address the 30.1% renter rate as a constituency with distinct interests from homeowners: younger renters and working-class households renting in PA-HD-171 have different concerns around eviction protection, housing affordability, and service access than the homeowner majority — acknowledging this internally divided base prevents a future challenger from organizing renters around neglect.",
          "Leverage the 42.5-year median age and working-class income profile with concrete legislative focus on rural healthcare access, manufacturing and skilled-trades workforce development, and property tax relief for fixed-income homeowners — these are the issues that will determine whether HD-171 remains safely Republican or becomes genuinely competitive when the next Democratic challenger emerges."
