          { name: "Assuming Demographic Diversity Automatically Translates to Coalition Stability", tag: "avoid", why: "A district that is 50.24% non-white but ran unopposed in 2024 cannot assume that demographic diversity automatically sustains a Democratic coalition in future cycles. Hispanic/Latino voters, Black voters, and Asian voters have distinct economic and policy priorities that may not align automatically — housing affordability may be the primary concern for renters, but small business access and education funding may drive different communities' votes differently. Any incumbent or challenger who treats 'diverse constituency' as a monolith rather than engaging each demographic community's specific policy concerns is building a fragile coalition vulnerable to defection when competing candidates offer more tailored constituent responses." }
