          { name: "Assuming That Latino Majority Support Is Automatic or Inherited", tag: "avoid", why: "While 64.73% Latino composition creates demographic alignment with Democratic registration, Latino voter participation is contingent on perception of concrete benefit and direct constituent service — not inherited party loyalty. Immigration policy, workplace protections, language access in public services, and economic opportunity for Spanish-speaking workers are the material governance concerns for the Latino majority, and a representative who defaults to generic Democratic positioning rather than specific Latino-community engagement will find turnout and mobilization capacity eroding as constituents perceive that their specific needs are not driving legislative priority." }
