          "Monitor and prevent primary challenge vulnerability: a well-organized primary opponent who commits to more aggressive constituent service, neighborhood visibility, and multiethnic organizing can exploit any gap between the unopposed result and actual community satisfaction; staying ahead of primary challenge requires continuous community investment."
