          "Do not treat 53% as a safe majority: in a district where college-educated, affluent voters have nationally demonstrated capacity to shift toward Democratic candidates on governance and cultural issues, a 6-point margin is functionally competitive and requires active engagement with the opposition's driving concerns, not consolidation of the existing Republican base."
