          { name: "Treating 64% as a Durable Floor Rather Than a Contingent Margin", tag: "avoid", why: "A 64% result in a suburban district is substantial but not exceptional for Pennsylvania Republicans — and it reflects current alignment on quality-of-life governance, not inherited loyalty or demographic destiny. If Gregory defaults to maintaining the existing coalition without demonstrating continued competence on schools, taxes, and infrastructure, the constituency will reassess. Complacency around a two-to-one margin in a district capable of sophisticated evaluation is precisely the posture that allows a credible challenger to erode support in a single cycle." },
          { name: "Ideological Positioning Over Suburban Pragmatism", tag: "avoid", why: "Affluent suburban voters, particularly college-educated ones, are primarily motivated by pragmatic governance and fiscal competence rather than ideological consistency. Any communication strategy that emphasizes partisan ideology over demonstrated results on suburban-specific issues — school quality, tax fairness, infrastructure adequacy — is misaligned with the constituency's actual decision-making framework. This voter population will punish perceived ideological rigidity or indifference to their material concerns, regardless of the politician's partisan affiliation." }
