          "Lead with school funding and education outcomes: in a district with 53.6% college education and a 43.2 median age, parents and professionals evaluate representatives directly on whether schools are adequately funded and whether children's educational prospects are improving—this is the highest-leverage constituent concern and the primary way either candidate can shift affluent voter preference.",
          "Address property tax and fiscal responsibility with specificity: at $109,350 income and 79% homeownership, voters in PA-SD-37 are acutely sensitive to property tax policy, municipal cost management, and whether state government is controlling spending responsibly—generic fiscal conservatism is insufficient; voters need concrete answers about where their tax dollars go and what results they produce.",
          "Recognize that college-educated suburban voters are genuinely persuadable: a 53-47 margin in a district this prosperous and educated reflects a constituency that evaluates based on candidate quality and governance performance rather than partisan identity—this is a seat where a credible challenger with a compelling case on education, fiscal management, or local governance can shift significant numbers of incumbent voters."
